  "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n| | $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ | |  | | $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ | |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{X}(x)$ | $0.3$ | $0.7$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.2$ | $0.8$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $P(X=1,Y=1)=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$\n- $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n- $X$ and $Y$ are independent",
